  "summary": "Skills collection bundling third-party install scripts and HTTP tooling",
  "details": "Package bundles a collection of 'skills' containing helper scripts in various languages. Static pattern matches fire on benign shapes: bundled-skills/rclone-cli/scripts/install.sh runs `curl https://rclone.org` to install the official rclone CLI from its vendor domain; bundled-skills/youtube-notetaker/scripts/verify.sh issues curl GET requests to verify endpoints; bundled-skills/junta-leiloeiros/scripts/*.py contain `ping` and GET/POST tokens in a web-scraping helper; bundled-skills/loki-mode/benchmarks/run-benchmarks.sh contains an `install` token and a curl line. No lifecycle hook in the package manifest reaches these scripts on `npm install`, no hardcoded attacker C2 is present, no installer secret paths (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, browser or wallet stores) are read, and no obfuscated fetch-and-execute path is present. The flagged patterns are documented tool-install and scraping/verification helpers bundled as skill assets, not an exfiltration or dropper mechanism against the installer.",
